# Fit the viewport (no clipped content)

Before finishing any trainer / exercise UI change, **verify the full task is visible** in a normal desktop viewport (~1280×800 and up) without cutting off questions, options, gaps, or footer actions.

## Hard ban (also see `no-mushy-layout.mdc`)

- Tip / answer key drawn **over** options or inputs
- Footer covering the last question
- Labels stacked on the same pixels

## Required check (do this every time)

1. Open the changed step mentally or in the browser.
2. Ask: **Is any learner text or control cut off at the bottom or side?**
3. Ask: **Is there empty background beside or below the content that could hold that clipped text?**
4. If yes to both → **layout bug**. Fix before shipping.

A Windows scrollbar next to empty dark space is always wrong (see also `no-useless-scroll.mdc`).

## How to fix (prefer in order)

1. **Compact panel mode** — short steps must use `flow-panel--compact` (or `--passage` / `--tech` / `--speak`); never `flex: 1` on the panel. See `compact-flow-panels.mdc`.
2. **Use horizontal space** — two columns, side bank/chips, wider shell (`max-width` not 960px on a full-bleed panel).
2. **Tighten** — smaller type, padding, gaps, `min-height`; drop decorative empty rows.
3. **One scroll pane only** if content is truly longer than the viewport (long essay / long passage) — never scroll a short quiz that would fit after tightening.

## Do not

- Leave `max-width: 960px` (or similar) on a panel that sits in a wider shell while content clips vertically.
- Stack long lists in one narrow column when the right half of the screen is empty.
- Ship with Q3+ options / last gaps / Check button half-visible.

## Graphs / textbook visuals

- Axis years and figures must be **high contrast** (near-black on cream plots), not dim grey.
- Match coursebook layout where provided (legend position, axis labels, scale).
